cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite the manuscript and the MedMNIST dataset."
title: "When Should a Medical Image Classifier Abstain? A Cross-Modality Benchmark of Selective Prediction"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Zhaoyang
    affiliation: "Henan Polytechnic University, Jiaozuo, Henan, China"
    email: 212603010048@home.hpu.edu.cn
year: 2026
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Benchmark of eight abstention scores (maximum softmax probability, predictive
  entropy, temperature scaling, the top-1/top-2 margin, Monte-Carlo dropout, deep
  ensembles, and split conformal LAC and APS scored by prediction-set size) on twelve
  MedMNIST 2D subsets covering eleven diagnostic modalities, with three seeds at
  28x28 and two seeds at 128x128. Reports both a post-hoc and a validation-frozen
  operating point for every score, and quantifies the validation-to-test transfer gap.
  Includes the released logit bundles so every reported number can be recomputed on
  CPU.
version: 1.1.0
references:
  - type: article
    title: "MedMNIST v2 - A large-scale lightweight benchmark for 2D and 3D biomedical image classification"
    authors:
      - family-names: Yang
        given-names: Jiancheng
    year: 2023
    journal: Scientific Data
    doi: 10.1038/s41597-022-01721-8
